      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HORATIUS SPECULO (3) worked to get to the lead and kept finding to score last time out when resuming over 2579m at this track, getting home by 9 metres. Sure to enjoy an economical run from this draw. Leading hope in a similar race. WAVES OF CHANCE (4) finished second last start over 2579m at this track, beaten 9 metres, after a good win at Launceston the run prior. Won't find this any harder and he can bounce back to winning form. WATERMELON SUGAR NZ (1) was in the money two starts ago then things went amiss last start when he broke and finished 10 metres away in fifth over 2200m at Launceston. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Beautifully placed and is able to make amends. MAEBEE (8) is worth plenty of thought off a last-start win by 1.2 metres at Launceston over 2200m.",
